WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.970
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.940
Today I am going to show you a paper and I
am almost out of words.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.820
It is so good.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.910
You know what, let’s jump right in.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:20.090
This new AI is very much like DALL-E 2, which
is a text to image AI.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.269
Our text goes in, an image comes out.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:28.859
And this new paper is not text to image, but
music.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:35.309
Yes, a piece of text goes in, and some hopefully
amazing music comes out.

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:37.570
Now, let’s see what it can do.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.969
Let’s ask for an epic soundtrack with orchestral
instruments.

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:47.190
And, do we let the AI get away with such a
simple prompt?

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.730
Of course not!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:55.640
The piece should build tension, and create
a sense of urgency, and you know what?

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.870
Add an a capella chorus on top of it.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:04.280
There is no way that an AI could generate
something like that, right?

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:23.670
Well, hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,
and listen.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.000
That was incredible.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.470
We will see in a moment how incredible exactly.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.030
Now let’s give this AI an even harder time.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:41.200
Oh yes, we wish for a bass and drums led reggae
song, with electric guitar, very difficult.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.969
But it gets even worse.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:44.969
Vocals.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:48.270
Expressive vocals with a laid-back style.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.670
There is absolutely no way that this is happening.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:02:14.379
But just in case, let’s listen.

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:19.800
I can’t believe it.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:27.310
Electric guitars, checkmark, I loved the intonation
and the personality, and the vocals were also

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.790
something else.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.790
Wow.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.569
Now, let’s ask for something completely
different.

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:55.830
We are real scholars, so we are going to ask
for real, 8-bit arcade music.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:02.510
Holy mother of papers, now that’s a song
that has momentum, intensity, a great guitar

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.510
riff.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.250
I am truly stunned.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.520
The prompt also asked for unexpected sounds.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.830
I have to admit I am not sure about that part,
but the rest was incredible.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:19.930
But not as incredible as these four other
things that is can also do.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:26.330
One, we already know that we can ask for some
piano playing, but it gets better.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:36.610
We can ask it to be a beginner piano player,
or a real pro.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:48.580
Let’s see.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.630
Now that’s super cool, loving it.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.640
Two, these were only 30-second sequences.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.780
Most songs are significantly longer than that,
and there is a problem with that.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.940
What is the problem?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:07.330
The problem is that these AI-based techniques
have trouble with long-term coherence.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:13.069
That means that a couple minutes into the
song, they don’t quite remember what they

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:14.069
played.

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:19.641
And that is indeed a problem, because writing
music is about building up a melody, and we

00:04:19.641 --> 00:04:24.060
have to remember the melody and embellish
it over time.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.220
So, what can this one offer in this area?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.650
What’s this?

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.340
You are kidding right?

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.330
A 5-minute long song?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:39.160
Well, let’s give it a shot, we will listen
to small snippets of this jazz song from different

00:04:39.160 --> 00:05:04.810
parts.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.970
Now this was truly something.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:13.810
For about 3 minutes, it felt like one coherent
song, and after that, it did not morph into

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.160
another one, but I feel that it lost some
coherence.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.750
However, it was not too far.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.990
Let’s say that this was 1.5 songs.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:29.470
That is an insane result because many previous
techniques could barely stay coherent for

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.150
even a few seconds.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.400
A few minutes is science fiction region.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.900
And all this, just one more paper down the
line.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.370
My goodness.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:43.830
Three, it can even image what paintings would
sound like.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:49.800
I have to admit that I did not find these
samples too convincing, however, the one for

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:58.660
Starry Night was pretty good.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:10.600
This is tranquil, soothing song, with a hint
of mysteriousness.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.960
It’s not perfect, but I like it a great
deal.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:21.389
And I think the capability is there for all
of these paintings, it is truly up to us humans

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:24.790
writing a good prompt to make them come alive.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:31.410
But wait, four what happens if we write a
prompt and we don’t quite like the results?

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.660
Well, it can generate several variants.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.190
In fact, as many as you wish.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:42.180
So, I promised that I would tell you how good
it exactly it.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.069
So how do we know that?

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.780
Well, through a user study.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:52.690
Get some humans in the room, show them some
real music, some AI music from this technique

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:57.840
and from previous works, and see which one
they like best.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.190
And the results are truly something else.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:05.420
MusicCaps is real music, so that should win
most of the time.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.160
That is not surprising.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:13.710
However, what is really surprising is that
it does not win all the time, and it gets

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:14.820
even better.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.480
Look at that!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:20.690
The new technique, MusicLM is rapidly closing
in.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:27.880
And remember, DALL-E 1 was an okay text to
image AI, and just one more paper down the

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.440
line, this is what DALL-E 2 was capable of.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:38.770
And with all this, I am convinced that we
are at a DALL-E 2 moment for music generation.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.430
It only gets better from here on out.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:46.810
And just imagine what we will be able to do
two more papers down the line.

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.520
What a time to be alive!

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.590
So, what do you think?

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.409
What prompts would you like to try in the
future?

00:07:53.409 --> 00:07:57.080
And what paintings would you like to come
to life?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:36.209
Let me know in the comments below!

00:08:36.209 --> 00:08:45.860
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

